+Dependencies: Same finite-class public-exogenous model as the finite-grid identity; signed minimax values; grid \(G_K=\{0,1/K,\ldots,(K-1)/K\}\); comparator for the continuum value uses \(\sup_{a\in[0,1]}\).
+Evidence: For every \(a\in[0,1]\), let \(\lfloor a\rfloor_K\in G_K\) be downward rounding, with \(a=1\) rounded to \((K-1)/K\). Pathwise, for \(M_t=\max_{s>t}P_s\),
+\[
+a{\bf 1}\{M_t>a\}
+\le
+\lfloor a\rfloor_K{\bf 1}\{M_t>\lfloor a\rfloor_K\}+1/K.
+\]
+Hence \(V_\theta\le V_\theta^{G_K}+T/K\). Also rounding every action of any continuum policy loses at most \(T/K\) expected reward in every world. These two inequalities give
